cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "DEPict: an open-source tri-modal platform for microplastic polymer identification"
message: "If you use this software or hardware, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: DEPict
    family-names: Contributors
repository-code: "https://github.com/your-org/DEPict"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - microplastics
  - dielectrophoresis
  - impedance-spectroscopy
  - computer-vision
  - sensor-fusion
  - environmental-monitoring
abstract: >
  DEPict is an open-source, sub-$400 platform that identifies the polymer type of
  microplastic particles by fusing dielectrophoresis, impedance spectroscopy, and
  computer vision with on-device machine learning, as an affordable alternative to
  FTIR spectroscopy.
